A reactive `if` among a flow's spans re-renders the flow on fyne and gtk4.

passReactivity makes a reactive `if` a render slot, and the slot's entries are
rendered into the node it sits in -- here a span or a flow. html renders a slot
into a `display:contents` wrapper and so into a span as readily as a box, and
says so with `#[gen.can(inlineSlots)]`. fyne and gtk4 have no such container: a
fyne flow is one widget over a tree of spans that are not canvas objects, so
the slot's func did not build (`*fynetext.Span does not implement
fyne.CanvasObject`), and a gtk4 flow is one label whose spans are no widgets at
all, so the slot appended a node nothing declared (`undefined: __n0`).

Withholding the grant, the flow holding the `if` is the slot instead: it is
wrapped in a one-pass loop over a const, which re-renders its whole body on
any state the body reads, and the `if` in it is ordinary. fyne builds the flow
with the `if` in place; gtk4's markup guards the runs with `gtk4rt.When`,
where it used to write them unconditionally.

deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `"quiet <b>LOUD</b>` -- the guarded run is not written unconditionally
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:test"
import md "sngl:ui/markup"

output {
    go {
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

component main node {
    var loud = true

    vbox {
        md.paragraph {
            md.text(value="quiet ")
            if loud {
                md.bold {
                    md.text(value="LOUD")
                }
            } else {
                md.italic {
                    md.text(value="soft")
                }
            }
            md.text(value=" end")
        }
        button #flip(text="flip", @click { loud = !loud })
    }
}

func testFlip(t Test, c main) {
    c.flip.click()
    t.assert(!c.loud)
}

window {
    main
}
